--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Charging/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the iOS +
macOS app targets list `Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,
feature-views,misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The
repo's real, compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**`,
where every sibling P7 page ships (Admin/*, Analytics/*, Automations/*, Battery/*) and
which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups).
The page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Charging/**`, the faithful
equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Charging`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the identical
reconciliation every sibling page log recorded; it is the only deviation from the literal
prompt path.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/charging/:id` is a DETAIL route carrying a session id, and
the flat top-level `AppRoute` registry hosts only parameter-less destinations. Following
the sibling detail-screen pattern (Automations PresetGallery/AutomationCard/...), the page
is exposed as a typed `NavigationDestination` for a `ChargingDetailLink(sessionID:)` value
via `View.chargingDetailDestination()` (ChargingDetailRouteRegistration.swift). The app
shell's `RouteHost` adopts `.chargingDetailDestination()` so every sidebar/detail/tab
NavigationStack resolves the link and the page is reachable + deep-linkable from the
existing `.charging` route. `ChargingDetailRouteRegistration.make(sessionID:)` mirrors the
sibling `…RouteRegistration` factory for hosts that want a ready-built screen. (Navigation
registration — AppShell.swift — is an allowed file per the prompt.)

